/-
# Infinite simple groups needing three generators (Kourovka Notebook Problem 6.44)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 6.44 (J. Wiegold): construct a finitely
generated infinite simple group requiring more than two generators.
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Finiteness
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Subgroup.Simple

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.InfiniteSimpleNotTwoGeneratedKourovka6Problem44Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 6.44 (J.
Wiegold). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700387 (`KOU-6.44`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

'Construct' is read as existence. Simple is Mathlib's `IsSimpleGroup`.
-/

/-- Kourovka 6.44 (J. Wiegold): there is a finitely generated infinite simple group that is not
generated by any two elements. -/
def existsFGInfiniteSimpleNotTwoGenerated : Prop :=
  ∃ (G : Type) (_ : Group G), Group.FG G ∧ Infinite G ∧ IsSimpleGroup G ∧
    ∀ a b : G, Subgroup.closure {a, b} ≠ ⊤

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive records that Guba (1986) constructed a finitely generated
infinite simple group that is not generated by any two elements. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D.
Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue,
arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 6.44 (J. Wiegold); resolution: V. S.
Guba, A finitely generated simple group with free 2-generated subgroups, Siberian Math. J. 27
(1986), 670-684, main result (zbMATH review Zbl 0616.20013): a finitely generated simple group in
which every 2-generated subgroup is free, hence an infinite finitely generated simple group
requiring more than two generators; Kourovka Archive, Problem 6.44: This has been done (Guba),
https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00969195.
-/
public theorem_wanted existsFGInfiniteSimpleNotTwoGenerated_holds :
    existsFGInfiniteSimpleNotTwoGenerated

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.InfiniteSimpleNotTwoGeneratedKourovka6Problem44Wanted
